    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n2 3 10\n5\n1 2 3 4 5\n2\n5 9\n4\n2 3 10 11",
        "output": "4 1\n1 2\n2 1\n0.5 2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The only possible assignment at all is to assign all the elves to the same toy.\nThe elves will meet at point 666, with the maximum distance traveled being 444. It can be shown that this is optimal.\nTest case 222: Group the first three elves and the last two elves. The maximum distance traveled by any elf will be 111. It can be shown that this is optimal.\nTest case 444: Group the first two and last two elves, who will meet at points 2.52.52.5 and 10.510.510.5 respectively. The maximum distance traveled by any elf is 0.50.50.5, which is optimal; and it isn't possible to achieve this with less than two toys."
      }
